{% comment %}
  Image with text. One image and one block of copy, with the text on any side.

  Media style covers the two treatments in the reference designs:
    - Simple:  just the image.
    - Panel:   a colored rectangle offset behind the image.
    - Overlap: a second image on the outer corner of the text pane.

  The copy and the overlapping image are one group. They sit side by side in
  normal flow inside the content pane — not the section — so the pair travels
  together when the image moves, and the overlap always anchors to the edge of
  the pane furthest from the main image.

  The heading has three placements, and they differ in what it is a sibling of:
    - Above:            a sibling of the group, so Content spacing can pin it to
                        the top of the pane and drop the group to the bottom.
    - With the text:    inside the group, above the divider, so it travels with
                        the copy and the second image as one block.
    - Over the section: out of flow, centered across the whole section.

  Image position says which side the picture is on; Text position says where the
  group sits down the pane, which only shows when the two are side by side.

  Content and media are emitted in visual order, so DOM order always matches
  what is on screen and focus order follows it — that is why the position is a
  Liquid branch rather than a CSS `order`.

  This section omits the canonical Display / Direction / Columns / Alignment /
  Position settings: it is a fixed two-part layout, so they cannot apply.
  Image position, Text position, and Media width replace them. Everything else — Size,
  Appearance, Borders, Padding, and Gap — is the shared layout verbatim.
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign media_style = s.media_style | default: 'simple'
  assign image = s.image

  comment
    Stated as where the image goes, because that is how the layout is read: the
    picture is on one side and everything else is on the other.
  endcomment
  assign image_side = s.image_position | default: 'left'

  case s.media_width
    when 'one_third'
      assign media_track = '33%'
    when 'two_thirds'
      assign media_track = '66%'
    else
      assign media_track = '50%'
  endcase

  comment
    Emitted in visual order so focus order follows the page. The content comes
    first whenever the image is on the far side of it.
  endcomment
  assign content_first = false
  if image_side == 'right' or image_side == 'bottom'
    assign content_first = true
  endif

  assign columns = 'minmax(0, 1fr)'
  if image_side == 'left'
    assign columns = media_track | append: ' minmax(0, 1fr)'
  elsif image_side == 'right'
    assign columns = 'minmax(0, 1fr) ' | append: media_track
  endif

  assign has_button = false
  if s.button_label != blank
    assign has_button = true
  endif

  comment
    The overlap hugs the edge of the pane furthest from the image. Stacked above
    or below there is no outer side, so it falls back to the end.
  endcomment
  assign overlap_side = 'end'
  if image_side == 'right'
    assign overlap_side = 'start'
  endif

  assign has_overlap = false
  if media_style == 'overlap' and s.secondary_image != blank
    assign has_overlap = true
  endif

  comment
    Three placements, and they differ in what the heading is a sibling of.
    "Above" makes it a sibling of the group, so Content spacing can push the two
    apart; "With the text" puts it inside the group, above the divider, so it
    travels with the copy and the overlapping image as one block; "Over the
    section" takes it out of flow entirely.
  endcomment
  assign heading_place = s.heading_position | default: 'inline'

  assign heading_overlay = false
  if heading_place == 'overlay'
    assign heading_overlay = true
  endif

  assign heading_with_text = false
  if heading_place == 'with_text'
    assign heading_with_text = true
  endif
%}

<div {% render 'layout-style', s: section.settings, class: 'image-with-text full-width' %}>
  {% render 'layout-background', s: section.settings %}

  <div class="layout__content">
    <div
      class="
        image-text
        image-text--image-{{ image_side }}
        image-text--block-{{ s.content_block | default: 'center' }}
        image-text--media-{{ media_style }}
        image-text--ratio-{{ s.image_ratio | default: 'adapt' }}
        image-text--align-{{ s.content_alignment | default: 'left' }}
        image-text--spacing-{{ s.content_spacing | default: 'grouped' }}
        image-text--overlap-{{ overlap_side }}
        {% if heading_overlay %}image-text--heading-overlay{% endif %}
      "
      style="
        --image-text-columns: {{ columns }};
        --panel-color: {{ s.panel_color | default: '#1F3A34' }};
        --panel-offset: {{ s.panel_offset | default: 32 }}px;
        --secondary-width: {{ s.secondary_image_width | default: 30 }}%;
      "
    >
      {%- capture media_markup -%}
        <div class="image-text__media">
          {%- if media_style == 'panel' -%}
            <span class="image-text__panel" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if image != blank -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign focal = image.presentation.focal_point | default: 'center center'
              assign focal_style = 'object-position: ' | append: focal | append: ';'
              assign alt = image.alt | default: ''
            -%}
            {{
              image
              | image_url: width: 2000
              | image_tag:
                class: 'image-text__image',
                widths: '375, 550, 750, 1100, 1500, 2000',
                sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw',
                alt: alt,
                loading: 'lazy',
                style: focal_style
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'image-text__image image-text__placeholder' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- capture content_markup -%}
        <div class="image-text__pane">
          {%- comment -%}
            The heading is a sibling of the body, not a child of it, so Content
            spacing can push the two apart. In overlay mode it is hoisted out of
            the pane entirely — see below.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if s.heading != blank and heading_place == 'inline' -%}
            <h2 class="image-text__heading">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Copy and the second image sit side by side in normal flow. Nothing
            here is positioned, so the row grows with its content and the two
            never collide.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="image-text__row">
            <div class="image-text__content">
              <div class="image-text__body">
                {%- comment -%}
                  Inside the group, so the heading stays with the copy and the
                  overlapping image rather than sitting apart from them.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if s.heading != blank and heading_with_text -%}
                  <h2 class="image-text__heading">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if s.show_divider -%}
                  <span class="image-text__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if s.text != blank -%}
                  <div class="image-text__text rte">{{ s.text }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if has_button -%}
                  <a
                    {% if s.button_link != blank %}
                      href="{{ s.button_link }}"
                    {% else %}
                      href="#"
                      aria-disabled="true"
                    {% endif %}
                    class="button{% if s.button_style == 'secondary' %} button--secondary{% endif %}"
                  >
                    {{- s.button_label -}}
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- if has_overlap -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign second = s.secondary_image
                assign second_focal = second.presentation.focal_point | default: 'center center'
                assign second_style = 'object-position: ' | append: second_focal | append: ';'
                assign second_alt = second.alt | default: ''
              -%}
              <div class="image-text__secondary">
                {{
                  second
                  | image_url: width: 1200
                  | image_tag:
                    class: 'image-text__secondary-image',
                    widths: '275, 360, 533, 720, 940, 1200',
                    sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 30vw, 100vw',
                    alt: second_alt,
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    style: second_style
                }}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Overlay heading. The only positioned element in the section, centered
        across the whole thing rather than over one column. Rendered first so it
        also comes first for a screen reader, matching the visual order.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.heading != blank and heading_overlay -%}
        <h2 class="image-text__heading image-text__heading--overlay">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if content_first -%}
        {{ content_markup }}
        {{ media_markup }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ media_markup }}
        {{ content_markup }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .image-text {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--image-text-columns, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--layout-gap, 0);
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: inherit;
  }

  /* Fill makes the image span the section height, so the cells must stretch. */
  .image-text--ratio-fill {
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .image-text__media {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .image-text__image {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .image-text--ratio-square .image-text__image {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  }
  .image-text--ratio-portrait .image-text__image {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }
  .image-text--ratio-landscape .image-text__image {
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  }
  .image-text--ratio-fill .image-text__media,
  .image-text--ratio-fill .image-text__image {
    height: 100%;
  }

  .image-text__placeholder {
    background-color: var(--color-border);
    fill: var(--color-background);
  }

  /*
   * Offset panel. Sits behind the image, shifted up and to the outside, so the
   * image reads as layered on top of a colored plate.
   */
  .image-text__panel {
    position: absolute;
    inset: calc(var(--panel-offset) * -1) calc(var(--panel-offset) * -1)
      var(--panel-offset) var(--panel-offset);
    background-color: var(--panel-color);
  }

  /*
   * The pane is the content grid cell. It holds the copy and, when the overlap
   * style is on, the second image — so the overlap travels with Content
   * position instead of being pinned to the section.
   */
  .image-text__pane {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    align-content: stretch;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /*
   * Where the text group sits down the pane. Only visible when the pane is
   * taller than its contents, which is what an image beside it usually does.
   */
  .image-text--block-top .image-text__pane {
    align-content: start;
  }
  .image-text--block-center .image-text__pane {
    align-content: center;
  }
  .image-text--block-bottom .image-text__pane {
    align-content: end;
  }

  /*
   * Spread fills the pane to push the heading and body apart, so it has to win
   * over the block placement above rather than fight it.
   */
  .image-text--spacing-spread .image-text__pane {
    align-content: stretch;
  }

  .image-text__content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .image-text__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: inherit;
  }

  /*
   * Spread pushes the heading to the top of the pane and the body to the
   * bottom. It only has an effect when the pane is taller than the copy, which
   * is why it needs the heading to be a separate element.
   */
  .image-text--spacing-spread .image-text__content {
    justify-content: space-between;
    height: 100%;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .image-text--align-left .image-text__content {
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-self: start;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .image-text--align-center .image-text__content {
    align-items: center;
    justify-self: center;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .image-text--align-right .image-text__content {
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-self: end;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .image-text--align-left .image-text__body {
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .image-text--align-center .image-text__body {
    align-items: center;
  }
  .image-text--align-right .image-text__body {
    align-items: flex-end;
  }

  .image-text__heading,
  .image-text__text {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /*
   * Overlay heading. Centered across the whole section rather than over one
   * column, and taken out of flow so the columns keep their own heights.
   *
   * `pointer-events: none` keeps it from swallowing clicks on whatever sits
   * beneath — it is display type, never a control.
   */
  .image-text__heading--overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: 0;
    inset-inline-start: 50%;
    z-index: 3;
    translate: -50% 0;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: min(100%, 40rem);
    pointer-events: none;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Room for the overlay so it never lands on top of the copy. */
  .image-text--heading-overlay .image-text__pane {
    padding-block-start: var(--overlay-heading-space, 8rem);
  }

  .image-text__divider {
    display: block;
    width: 8.75rem;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /*
   * Copy and the second image, side by side in normal flow. The image sits on
   * the outer side, so it swaps with Content position rather than staying put.
   */
  .image-text__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--layout-gap, 0);
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }

  .image-text--overlap-start .image-text__row {
    flex-direction: row-reverse;
  }

  /*
   * The group — copy, and the overlapping image beside it — is one block. It
   * ends up bottom-aligned so the second image sits on the baseline of the
   * text, which is what makes the pair read as a single composition.
   */
  .image-text__row {
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .image-text__secondary {
    flex: 0 0 var(--secondary-width);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .image-text__row .image-text__content {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }

  .image-text__secondary-image {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .image-text {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .image-text__content {
      max-width: none;
    }

    /* No room to spread vertically on a phone; let the copy sit together. */
    .image-text--spacing-spread .image-text__content {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      height: auto;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    /* Copy above, second image below — no room for them side by side. */
    .image-text__row,
    .image-text--overlap-start .image-text__row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .image-text__secondary {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }

    .image-text--heading-overlay .image-text__pane {
      padding-block-start: 5rem;
    }

    .image-text__panel {
      inset: calc(var(--panel-offset) * -0.5) calc(var(--panel-offset) * -0.5)
        calc(var(--panel-offset) * 0.5) calc(var(--panel-offset) * 0.5);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.image_with_text",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.content" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "t:labels.heading", "default": "t:defaults.image_text_heading" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "text", "label": "t:labels.text", "default": "t:defaults.image_text_text" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_divider", "label": "t:labels.show_divider", "default": false },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "t:labels.button_label", "default": "t:defaults.shop_collection" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button_link", "label": "t:labels.button_link" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "button_style", "label": "t:labels.button_style", "default": "primary",
      "options": [
        { "value": "primary", "label": "t:options.button_style.primary" },
        { "value": "secondary", "label": "t:options.button_style.secondary" }
      ] },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.media" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "t:labels.image" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "image_ratio", "label": "t:labels.image_ratio", "default": "landscape",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "t:options.image_ratio.adapt" },
        { "value": "square", "label": "t:options.image_ratio.square" },
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "t:options.image_ratio.portrait" },
        { "value": "landscape", "label": "t:options.image_ratio.landscape" },
        { "value": "fill", "label": "t:options.image_ratio.fill" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_style", "label": "t:labels.media_style", "default": "simple",
      "options": [
        { "value": "simple", "label": "t:options.media_style.simple" },
        { "value": "panel", "label": "t:options.media_style.panel" },
        { "value": "overlap", "label": "t:options.media_style.overlap" }
      ] },
    { "type": "color", "id": "panel_color", "label": "t:labels.panel_color", "default": "#1F3A34",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.media_style == 'panel' }}" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "panel_offset", "label": "t:labels.panel_offset", "min": 8, "max": 96, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 32,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.media_style == 'panel' }}" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "secondary_image", "label": "t:labels.secondary_image", "info": "t:info.secondary_image",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.media_style == 'overlap' }}" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "secondary_image_width", "label": "t:labels.secondary_image_width", "min": 15, "max": 50, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 30,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.media_style == 'overlap' }}" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.layout" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "image_position", "label": "t:labels.image_position", "info": "t:info.image_position", "default": "left",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "t:options.alignment.left" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "t:options.alignment.right" },
        { "value": "top", "label": "t:options.position.top" },
        { "value": "bottom", "label": "t:options.position.bottom" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "content_block", "label": "t:labels.text_position", "info": "t:info.text_position", "default": "center",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.image_position == 'left' or section.settings.image_position == 'right' }}",
      "options": [
        { "value": "top", "label": "t:options.position.top" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:options.position.center" },
        { "value": "bottom", "label": "t:options.position.bottom" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_width", "label": "t:labels.media_width", "default": "half",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.image_position == 'left' or section.settings.image_position == 'right' }}",
      "options": [
        { "value": "one_third", "label": "t:options.media_width.one_third" },
        { "value": "half", "label": "t:options.media_width.half" },
        { "value": "two_thirds", "label": "t:options.media_width.two_thirds" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "content_alignment", "label": "t:labels.content_alignment", "default": "left",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "t:options.alignment.left" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:options.alignment.center" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "t:options.alignment.right" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "content_spacing", "label": "t:labels.content_spacing", "info": "t:info.content_spacing", "default": "grouped",
      "options": [
        { "value": "grouped", "label": "t:options.content_spacing.grouped" },
        { "value": "spread", "label": "t:options.content_spacing.spread" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "heading_position", "label": "t:labels.heading_position", "info": "t:info.heading_position", "default": "inline",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inline", "label": "t:options.heading_position.inline" },
        { "value": "with_text", "label": "t:options.heading_position.with_text" },
        { "value": "overlay", "label": "t:options.heading_position.overlay" }
      ] },
    { "type": "range", "id": "gap", "label": "t:labels.gap", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 48 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.size" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "width", "label": "t:labels.width", "default": "page",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page", "label": "t:options.width.page" },
        { "value": "full", "label": "t:options.width.full" }
      ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "height", "label": "t:labels.height", "default": "fit",
      "options": [
        { "value": "fit", "label": "t:options.height.fit" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:options.height.small" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:options.height.medium" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:options.height.large" },
        { "value": "full", "label": "t:options.height.full" }
      ] },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.appearance" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "t:labels.color_scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "background_media", "label": "t:labels.background_media", "default": "none",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:options.background_media.none" },
        { "value": "image", "label": "t:options.background_media.image" },
        { "value": "video", "label": "t:options.background_media.video" }
      ] },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "background_image", "label": "t:labels.background_image",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}" },
    { "type": "video", "id": "background_video", "label": "t:labels.background_video",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background_color", "label": "t:labels.background_color", "info": "t:info.background_color" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "background_overlay", "label": "t:labels.show_background_overlay", "default": false },
    { "type": "color", "id": "overlay_color", "label": "t:labels.overlay_color", "default": "#000000",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_overlay }}" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "overlay_opacity", "label": "t:labels.overlay_opacity", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_overlay }}" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:general.borders" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "border_style", "label": "t:labels.style", "default": "none",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:options.border_style.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:options.border_style.solid" }
      ] },
    { "type": "range", "id": "border_width", "label": "t:labels.border_width", "min": 1, "max": 8, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.border_style == 'solid' }}" },
